# Add inside the `{$DOMAIN} { ... }` site block in
# 3vnsystems-infrastructure/caddy/Caddyfile, alongside the existing
# product blocks and BEFORE the catch-all `handle { reverse_proxy
# homepage:80 }` at the end — Caddy matches handle blocks in order, and
# the catch-all would otherwise swallow these.
#
# The prefix is NOT in this file. Caddy reads it from the environment
# variable THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX when it loads the config, so it lives only
# on the server (see root-env.additions). The first prefix was written
# here, became public with the repository on 2026-11-15, and is retired:
# it is still in git history, which is why it was rotated, not just
# deleted. Never put a real prefix back in this file.

	# --- 3vn-robotics fleet view ---
	#
	# UNLISTED: the path is obscurity, not access control. Anyone given
	# the link can pass it on, and the read side has no login. Do not link
	# it from 3vnsystems-homepage, and keep `Disallow: /fleet-` in that
	# repo's robots.txt.
	#
	# If THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX is unset, the default below applies, so the
	# view lands on a known path instead of swallowing the whole site at
	# `/*`. If it is set but EMPTY, Caddy rejects the whole config at
	# `caddy validate` / `caddy reload` (`strip_prefix` gets no argument;
	# checked with Caddy 2.11.7), so the running config stays. Both are
	# loud; deploy/README.md step 8 has the check.
	#
	# The ingest endpoint is separate from the view on purpose. It is the
	# one thing robots POST to, it is authenticated by a bearer token,
	# and keeping it on its own path makes it obvious in access logs
	# which requests are machines and which are a person looking.
	@robotIngest path {$THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX:/fleet-prefix-not-set}/api/telemetry
	handle @robotIngest {
		uri strip_prefix {$THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX:/fleet-prefix-not-set}
		reverse_proxy threevn-fleet:8080
	}

	# The read-only view and its JSON. Same prefix strip: the Go service
	# registers its routes at the root and knows nothing about the
	# prefix, so rotating it means changing THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX (and the
	# fleet service's FLEET_BASE_PATH to match) and reloading Caddy.
	handle {$THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX:/fleet-prefix-not-set}/* {
		uri strip_prefix {$THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX:/fleet-prefix-not-set}
		reverse_proxy threevn-fleet:8080
	}

	redir {$THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX:/fleet-prefix-not-set} {$THREEVN_FLEET_PREFIX:/fleet-prefix-not-set}/ permanent
